The net folder is the client's online-multiplayer slice (Phase 7): it plays a match against the server-authoritative `/ws/kt` gateway (built in Phase 4) with NO local rules engine. kt-socket.ts is a thin transport — it opens a WebSocketLike via an injectable factory, serializes outgoing KtClientMessages, and validates every incoming frame with the engine's parseKtServerMessage before dispatching (a malformed frame is dropped, never thrown); no auto-reconnect in v1. The hooks/ subfolder's useKtMatch drives one connection: it sends `join` on open and holds only server-sent state (joined/snapshot/over frames replace the snapshot; error surfaces a message), guarding stale-socket late frames with a generation ref and sending `leave` on unmount. OnlineMatchScreen.tsx is the surface: a connect form (match id + server URL) then the reused controlled Arena rendered from snapshots, interactive only on the human's turn. kt-config.ts holds the Vite-env connection defaults (import.meta.env.VITE_KT_WS) and is jest-mapped to kt-config.stub.ts because jest runs CJS and cannot parse import.meta. The wire protocol + validators all live in the engine (net/protocol.ts) so client and server cannot drift.
